abel":"after 22.5 M frames \u00b7 full game","note":"seeds 12345-12354, protocol full","seconds":29.4,"replay":"replays/goal_goal_f022503k.gif"},{"t":"2026-11-09 01:36:05","kind":"checkpoint","frames":23003136,"path":"checkpoints/main/model_023003k.pt","score":"","run":"main"},{"t":"2026-11-09 01:29:33","kind":"checkpoint","frames":22503424,"path":"checkpoints/main/model_022503k.pt","score":412.0,"run":"main"},{"t":"2026-11-09 01:22:59","kind":"checkpoint","frames":22003712,"path":"checkpoints/main/model_022003k.pt","score":"","champion":"checkpoints/main/model_022003k.pt","run":"main","replay":"replays/main_0046.gif"},{"t":"2026-11-09 01:16:36","title":"Pre-registered: how the final result will be judged","text":"Written at 20.5 M frames, before any final results exist. (1) Candidates: the final 40 M checkpoint and the best two checkpoints by the 10-game checks from 30 M frames on. (2) For each candidate, a 100-game evaluation on fresh seeds (900000-900099), strict full-game protocol, gives its true level; the candidate with the highest 100-game mean is THE model. (3) The goal check for THE model is 10 full games on seeds 12345-12354 (the fixed check seeds), strict full-game protocol; it is reported together with its 100-game mean, so a lucky 10-game draw can't pass silently. The training-wrapper protocol is reported alongside. (4) If THE model's 100-game mean is below 300, training continues from the 40 M checkpoint as change 3 (a short extra schedule), as long as the deadline allows, and every result is reported. Context for these rules: at 20 M frames the 10-game check said 229.7, but 64 envpool games said 169.5 (standard error 17), and 16 gymnasium games 132.4 (standard error 26.5): consistent with each other within the noise, and far noisier than one 10-game check suggests.","kind":"journal"},{"t":"2026-11-09 01:16:16","kind":"checkpoint","frames":21504000,"path":"checkpoints/main/model_021504k.pt","score":172.0,"run":"main"},{"t":"2026-11-09 01:08:11","kind":