","frames":5001216,"n":10,"score":16.5,"std":4.600724580614087,"ci":[13.209068551306485,19.790931448693517],"min":9.0,"max":23.0,"scores":[9.0,19.0,23.0,19.0,20.0,14.0,17.0,20.0,14.0,10.0],"lengths":[411,702,807,654,821,484,619,613,581,495],"truncated":[false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false],"seed":12345,"greedy":false,"protocol":"wrappers","label":"after 5.0 M frames \u00b7 training wrappers","note":"seeds 12345-12354, protocol wrappers","seconds":12.2,"replay":"replays/goal_goal_f005001k_wrappers.gif"},{"kind":"goal_check","t":"2026-11-09 00:28:54","policy":"checkpoints/main/model_002502k.pt","frames":2502656,"n":10,"score":6.2,"std":2.043961295567452,"ci":[4.737939755003236,7.6620602449967645],"min":4.0,"max":10.0,"scores":[4.0,9.0,4.0,5.0,7.0,5.0,5.0,6.0,10.0,7.0],"lengths":[248,469,268,305,377,309,312,368,502,379],"truncated":[false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false],"seed":12345,"greedy":false,"protocol":"wrappers","label":"after 2.5 M frames \u00b7 training wrappers","note":"seeds 12345-12354, protocol wrappers","seconds":8.4,"replay":"replays/goal_goal_f002502k_wrappers.gif"},{"t":"2026-11-09 00:24:20","kind":"checkpoint","frames":18001920,"path":"checkpoints/main/model_018001k.pt","score":"","champion":"checkpoints/main/model_018001k.pt","run":"main","replay":"replays/main_0038.gif"},{"t":"2026-11-09 00:20:56","title":"Correction: the protocol gap is mostly noise","text":"A larger test of the 15 M model, 64 games per protocol on fresh seeds (777000+): 162.8 (standard error 13.1) with the training wrappers, 145.6 (standard error 14.8) on plain full games. The difference, about 17 points, is within the noise. The earlier 20-game comparison (185 vs 139) overstated it, and the 10-game goal check of 86.5 was simply a low draw. With a spread of about 110 points per game, a 10-game mean has a standard error of about 35 points. Both protocols stay in the goal checks. For the final goal, the model needs a true mean well above 300 to pass a 10-game check reliably.","kind":"journal"},{"t":"2026-11-09 00:16:20","title":"Change 2: goal checks now use two protocols","text":"At 15 M frames the training games averaged about 150-190 points, but the goal check scored 86.5. Testing the 15 M model on the same 20 seeds both ways explained it: 184.8 with the standard training wrappers (a lost life is an episode boundary with envpool's soft reset and automatic FIRE; the score is still the real score of the whole 5-life game, exactly what the training curve counts) and 138.7 on plain full games, where nothing happens at a lost life and the agent must relaunch the ball itself. Both are common ways to report Atari scores, and the goal's 'standard Atari wrappers' fits the first. To avoid picking the flattering one, every checkpoint check from now on runs both protocols on the same seeds (12345-12354), the site shows both, and the final claim will say which protocol it is. The earlier checks were all strict full-game checks. Note also how noisy 10 games are: on 10 games the same 15 M model scored 86.5, on 20 games 138.7.","kind":"journal"},{"t":"2026-11-09 00:16:19","kind":"checkpoint","frames":17502208,"path":"checkpoints/main/model_017502k.pt","score":"","run":"main"},{"t":"2026-11-09 00:08:41","kind":"checkpoint","frames":17002496,"path":"checkpoints/main/model_017002k.pt","score":"","run":"main"},{"t":"2026-11-09 00:02:10","kind":"checkpoint","frames":16502784,"path":"checkpoints/main/model_016502k.pt","score":"","run":"main"},{"kind":"goal_check","t":"2026-11-08 23:56:16","policy":"checkpoints/main/model_015003k.pt","frames":15003648,"n":10,"score":86.5,"std":23.632604596192948,"ci":[69.5954276185406,103.4045723814594],"min":48.0,"max":124.0,"scores":[89.0,96.0,111.0,124.0,75.0,89.0,48.0,92.0,90.0,51.0],"lengths":[1310,1570,1351,1515,1087,1423,716,1214,1407,1109],"truncated":[false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false,false],"seed":12345,"greedy":false,"label":"after 15.0 M frames \u00b7 